⚡🇺🇸 Bloomberg reports that the "circle debt" phenomenon in Ai investment continues to dominate the Ai industry.

In simple terms companies are lending each other debt to keep each other alive using their own inflated overvalued stocks as collateral. While using different methods like merges to get even more debt. 

@medmannews

⚡🇳🇿 A New Zealand Arms bill has just passed and is awaiting Royal assent and commencement later this year. The changes ease restrictions in some areas while adding them in others.

Changes of note include extending the gunsmith possession period for pistols and restricted firearms from 7 to 21 days without a permit, allowing multi-entry visitor licences for up to 18 months, granting museum workers five year licences (renewable for ten) without endorsement requirements, and reducing the annual scheduled pistol shooting activities needed to maintain an endorsement from 12 to 10. Urgent temporary licence suspensions are also enabled for domestic violence or self-harm risks, though current licensing, storage, and registry rules remain in force until official commencement dates.

